---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Chart from '../../components/Chart.astro';
import CaseNavigation from '../../components/CaseNavigation.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="CEG outreach experiment" description="Flyer design, distribution, and website activity analysis for Envision Arlington’s Civic Engagement Group, by Monalisa Hota.">
  <section class="page-intro"><h1>CEG outreach experiment</h1><p class="lead">A comparison of website activity around three civic outreach periods in Arlington.</p></section>
  <CaseNavigation />
  <div class="case-meta" id="overview"><div><span class="small">Organisation</span><p>Envision Arlington<br />Civic Engagement Group</p></div><div><span class="small">My involvement</span><p>December 2024 – May 2026</p></div><div><span class="small">My contribution</span><p>Flyer design, distribution planning, and data analysis</p></div></div>
  <section class="split"><div><h2>Background</h2></div><div><p>The Civic Engagement Group connects Arlington residents with opportunities to participate in town life.</p><p>I led an outreach experiment involving flyer design, distribution, and analysis of website activity. I compared unique visitors and site sessions around successive outreach periods.</p></div></section>
  <section class="feature split"><div><h2>The flyer</h2><p>I designed a flyer with local imagery, a meeting invitation, and a QR code linking residents to the CEG website to register.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${base}documents/ceg-outreach-flyer.pdf`}>View the flyer · PDF</a></div><a class="flyer-preview" href={`${base}documents/ceg-outreach-flyer.pdf`}><img src={`${base}images/ceg/flyer.webp`} alt="CEG outreach flyer with an Arlington meeting invitation and QR code" width="1400" height="1082" loading="lazy" /></a></section>
  <section id="outreach-periods"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Outreach periods</h2></div><div class="grid three timeline"><article><p class="small">18 April – 13 May 2025</p><h3>Spring outreach</h3><p>Website activity was higher after outreach. Monthly charts compare the period with earlier years.</p></article><article><p class="small">29 September – 18 October 2025</p><h3>Autumn outreach</h3><p>Flyer distribution was incomplete because flyers were taken down. Postcards were sent on 18 October.</p></article><article><p class="small">13 February 2026</p><h3>Postcards only</h3><p>A 30-day comparison shows fewer visitors afterward. Earlier February and March peaks provide seasonal context.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="evidence" id="website-activity"><h2>Website activity over time</h2><p class="measure-note"><strong>Reading the charts:</strong> bars represent unique visitors; red crosses represent site sessions, which can include repeat visits. Their axes are labelled separately. These are the original chart images.</p><Chart image="all-months" title="Website activity across the full period" alt="Monthly unique visitors and site sessions from May 2023 to May 2026, with outreach and seasonal annotations" caption="February and March have historically attracted higher traffic, possibly around town elections. The full timeline provides context for each outreach period." /></section>
  <section class="evidence" id="spring-2025"><h2>Spring 2025</h2><div class="finding"><strong>40 → 53</strong><p>Site sessions before and after outreach.<br /><small>The chart uses 60-day windows and excludes March from the pre-outreach comparison.</small></p></div><Chart image="phase1-before-after" title="Spring outreach: before and after" alt="Spring 2025 comparison: site sessions rise from 40 before outreach to 53 afterward; unique visitors also increase" caption="Unique visitors and revisits increased after 18 April 2025. March was excluded from the earlier window as a seasonal adjustment." /><Chart image="phase1-months" title="Spring outreach in its monthly context" alt="Monthly spring website traffic compared across years, with annotations about the 2025 outreach" caption="Monthly activity alongside prior years provides context for the shorter before/after comparison." /></section>
  <section class="evidence" id="autumn-2025"><h2>Autumn 2025</h2><Chart image="phase2-months" title="Autumn outreach: incomplete distribution" alt="August to October traffic across 2022–2025; annotations describe removed flyers and incomplete autumn outreach" caption="Flyers were taken down, with some remaining at Robbins Library and stores. Postcards were sent on 18 October. The chart shows no apparent traffic improvement associated with this phase." /></section>
  <section class="evidence" id="february-2026"><h2>February 2026</h2><div class="finding"><strong>30 → 18</strong><p>Unique visitors before and after postcard-only outreach.<br /><small>The chart compares 30-day windows around 13 February 2026.</small></p></div><Chart image="phase3-before-after" title="Postcards only: before and after" alt="Postcard-only comparison shows 30 unique visitors before 13 February 2026 and 18 afterward, with fewer site sessions too" caption="The post-outreach window shows fewer unique visitors and site sessions, unlike the spring comparison." /><Chart image="phase3-months" title="Postcards only in seasonal context" alt="January to March website activity across 2022–2026; annotation notes historically high February and March traffic" caption="Traffic has historically been higher at this time of year. February’s monthly total and the 30-day post-outreach count cover different windows and are not the same measure." /></section>
  <section class="reflection split" id="limitations"><div><h2>Limitations and next steps</h2></div><div><p>Seasonality, incomplete distribution, and different comparison windows affect the interpretation. These descriptive comparisons do not establish a causal effect or measure meeting attendance.</p><p>A future round could track distribution counts, campaign-specific QR links, and registrations alongside website activity.</p><p class="small">Source: the CEG flyer and six annotated chart images. No underlying dataset was supplied; figures quoted here are taken from chart labels.</p></div></section>
  <dialog class="chart-dialog" aria-labelledby="chart-title"><div class="dialog-header"><h2 id="chart-title">Chart detail</h2><button type="button" class="close-dialog" autofocus>Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button></div><div class="dialog-image"><img alt="" /></div><p class="small">On smaller screens, scroll horizontally to read the original chart.</p></dialog>
  <script>
    const dialog = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>('.chart-dialog');
    const image = dialog?.querySelector('img');
    const title = dialog?.querySelector('#chart-title');
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('.chart-zoom').forEach(link => {
      link.addEventListener('click', event => {
        if (!dialog || !image || !title || event.ctrlKey || event.metaKey || event.shiftKey || event.altKey) return;
        event.preventDefault();
        image.src = link.href;
        image.alt = link.querySelector('img')?.alt ?? '';
        title.textContent = link.dataset.caption ?? 'Chart detail';
        dialog.showModal();
      });
    });
    dialog?.querySelector('button')?.addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
    dialog?.addEventListener('click', event => { if (event.target === dialog) dialog.close(); });
  </script>
</Layout>
